     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum per dose of 850 mg to 1000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- Another dose you had in mind\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
